DETAILED PROJECT REPORT (DPR)Project Title: MicroPMS (Automated Hourly Hotel Management System)Deployment Target: Shared Linux Hosting (cPanel / Apache / LiteSpeed)Technology Stack: PHP 8.x, MySQL (InnoDB), Vanilla JS/Tailwind CSSExternal Integrations: Razorpay API v1, Meta WhatsApp Cloud API, Telegram Bot API1. Executive Summary & Business ObjectiveTraditional Property Management Systems (PMS) are structurally bound to 24-hour stay cycles, rendering them inefficient for transit hotels and micro-stay operators. MicroPMS is engineered to treat room inventory as dynamic time-blocks.By calculating stay durations down to the hour across date boundaries, the system allows a single room to be sold multiple times within a 24-hour window. To maintain low operational costs, the architecture is specifically designed to bypass the need for expensive VPS infrastructure, running entirely on standard shared web hosting using database transaction locking and cPanel cron jobs.2. System Architecture & Infrastructure TopologyTo ensure security on shared hosting, the system isolates core business logic from the public web directory.Directory Layout/home/pms_core/ (Secure Core): Houses database credentials, API keys, and the OperationalEngine logic./home/public_html/ (Public Web): Contains the mobile-first guest booking UI, the admin dashboard, and the Razorpay/Cron webhook endpoints.Process FlowGuest Input: Client selects check-in/out datetimes via a lightweight HTML5/Tailwind mobile web interface.Concurrency Check: PHP backend requests a strict MySQL row-lock (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) to ensure the room is available.Payment Bridge: A temporary database record (pending_hold) is created, and the Razorpay checkout overlay is launched.Asynchronous Fulfillment: Razorpay's server sends a webhook to webhook_razorpay.php, which finalizes the booking, marks the room as occupied, and triggers external WhatsApp/Telegram notifications via synchronous cURL requests.3. Database Schema (Entity-Relationship Model)The database utilizes MySQL InnoDB to leverage ACID-compliant transactions, critical for preventing double bookings.staff_users: Manages Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) with access_level (owner vs. front_desk).rooms: Tracks physical inventory and real-time state (clean, dirty, occupied).sliding_rates: Stores the custom hourly pricing configuration (e.g., 1 Hr = ₹400, 2 Hrs = ₹700).bookings: The core transactional table. Uses a heavy compound index (idx_collision_guard) on room_id, check_in, check_out, payment_status to ensure timeline search queries execute instantly.folio_ledger: A sub-ledger attached to each booking to track multiple payment events (e.g., the initial online Razorpay hold + a secondary cash payment at the desk).4. Core Functional ModulesModule A: The Cross-Date Algorithmic Pricing EngineCalculates the exact billing amount based on absolute timestamps. If a stay exceeds 24 hours, it splits the time into full days and residual hours.Mathematical Model: $\text{Total Cost} = (D \times P_{24}) + P_{H}$$D$ = Number of full 24-hour blocks.$P_{24}$ = Fixed base rate for a full day (e.g., ₹2,000).$P_{H}$ = Residual hours mapped to the configured sliding_rates table.Module B: The Razorpay Payment & State ControllerBecause shared hosting lacks Redis to temporarily lock rooms during checkout, MicroPMS manages state directly in MySQL. Bookings are initialized as pending_hold. If the Razorpay webhook confirms payment, it shifts to completed_paid. If the user abandons the checkout, a cron job sweeps and deletes the hold after 15 minutes.Module C: Automated Notification RelaysGuest (WhatsApp): Triggers instantly upon payment success with a booking summary. Triggers again exactly 30 minutes before the scheduled check-out time offering an extension link.Owner (Telegram): Acts as a live operational ticker. Sends alerts for new bookings, daily revenue summaries, and high-priority alerts if a guest overstays their timeframe.Module D: Administrative Folio & Front Desk ControlsProvides a mobile-friendly dashboard for staff to:View active room states (color-coded: Green = Clean, Red = Occupied, Orange = Dirty).Generate Razorpay "Payment Links" and dispatch them via WhatsApp to collect outstanding balances.Add manual cash/card transactions to a guest's folio_ledger.(Owner Only) Edit existing booking dates and modify the hourly pricing matrix.5. Automated Operational Workflows (Cron Scheduler)To replace persistent background workers, a single script (cron_scheduler.php) is executed by the cPanel cron engine every 5 minutes (*/5 * * * *).The 15-Minute Sweep: Reverts any pending_hold bookings older than 15 minutes back to available inventory.The Pre-Departure Warning: Scans for active bookings checking out within the next 30 minutes and dispatches the WhatsApp warning template.The Overstay Flag: Identifies bookings where the current time has surpassed the check_out time. It marks the room as dirty for housekeeping and alerts the owner via Telegram.6. Security & Risk MitigationRace Conditions (Double Booking): Mitigated by MySQL Pessimistic Locking. The database locks the specific room's timeline during the microsecond the system verifies availability, forcing simultaneous requests to queue and subsequently fail if the room is taken.Financial Spoofing: Mitigated by strict payload verification. The webhook_razorpay.php endpoint refuses any incoming POST request that does not match the cryptographic hash_hmac SHA256 signature generated by your private Razorpay Secret Key.7. Quality Assurance (QA) & Testing MatrixBefore production deployment, the system must pass these critical test thresholds:Test CategoryExecutionExpected ResultLogic BoundariesEnter a duration of 25 hours.Engine calculates $1 \times \text{Daily Rate} + 1 \times \text{Hourly Premium}$.Concurrency LoadFire 10 simultaneous API requests to book Room 101 for the exact same hour.1 request generates a payment link; 9 requests return HTTP 409 (Conflict).Webhook SecuritySend a forged success payload to the webhook endpoint.System rejects with HTTP 400. Booking status remains pending_hold.Cron ExecutionCreate a test booking that expires in 5 minutes. Wait 6 minutes.Room automatically flags as dirty. Telegram alert is received.RBAC EnforcementLog in as front_desk and attempt to modify the hourly price matrix via direct URL request.Request denied. Redirected to the standard dashboard.